{"kind":"artifact","text":"Bounded MCP status and wait, unmerged on branch task/status-projection at 5482674fba889a87bfd37b8efbc280b7d5baae80. The MCP tools returned the entire projection twice, once as structuredContent and again as pretty-printed JSON in the text block, so the cost of asking grew with the log while the answer an agent wanted stayed the same size. Status is now actor-oriented: what is waiting on you, what you are waiting on others for, the frontier and cursor, and which of your own acts the fold judged ineffective, that last because an act which silently failed to take force is what an agent is least likely to notice. Wait is delta-oriented, carrying the events after the caller's cursor, bounded to a fifty-event window with an explicit count of anything older it skipped. Neither narrows the record: the diff does not touch spike/internal at all, so /v0/status still serves the complete projection, the browser still reads it, gs status is unchanged, and a fresh clone still audits from the log. Every digest carries totals — depth, commitments by status, artifact and stale counts, ineffective acts, statement count — and names where the full projection lives, so summarising does not become hiding. The text block is a one-line summary rather than a second copy of the payload. Reset and degraded semantics are preserved on both the resident and local-sequencer paths, and a degraded status says so rather than inventing a live generation. Measured at depth 190 against the live workroom, counting the whole JSON-RPC line in UTF-8 without its terminating newline: status 614,232 to 7,748 bytes and wait 622,997 to 6,516, reductions of 98.7 and 99.0 percent. The test pins the property rather than the number — ten times the history may grow the digest only by the width of its own counters, while the projection it summarises grows linearly — because a fixed byte count would rot the moment anything else changed. make vet, make test, go test -race ./..., and make build pass. Not reviewed and not merged.","body":{"commit":"5482674fba889a87bfd37b8efbc280b7d5baae80","path":"spike/cmd/gitseq-mcp"}}